<BaseLayout title="Selling an island home" description="How Dana sells homes on the Kestrel Sound islands: pricing, inspections before listing, photos on a clear day, and help with the move." plainTop>
  <Prose pretitle="Selling" title="Selling an island home" lead="Island buyers ask hard questions about wells, septic and bluffs. A sale goes faster when the answers are ready before the first viewing." image="tile-aerial.webp" alt="A shingled waterfront house on a wooded point, seen from above">
    <h2>Before the listing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A price based on island sales from the last two years, not mainland averages.</li>
      <li>A well test and septic inspection done in advance, so buyers see the reports with the listing.</li>
      <li>Photos and a drone flight on the first clear day, even if that means waiting a week.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>While it is listed</h2>
    <p>Viewings are grouped around the ferry so buyers from the mainland can see your home and two others in one trip. You get a short note after every viewing: who came, what they liked, and what worried them.</p>
    <h2 id="moving">Moving help</h2>
    <p>Moving off an island takes planning: ferry reservations for the truck, a storage unit on the mainland, an estate sale for the furniture that will not fit. Dana keeps a list of movers, cleaners and caretakers who work on the islands, and books them for you.</p>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-solid" data-open-contact>Ask what your home is worth</button>
  </Prose>
</BaseLayout>
